  "scope": [
    "PBR resources capture each created pixel/attribute/index backing independently of mutable public collections. Close retires all geometry/material/texture owners, clears graph/texture references and private lookup, detaches only captured private buffers and clears closure collections.",
    "Constructor failure and source3 world wrapper preserve the original cause, including null, despite nested cleanup errors. Separate immutable preparation remains reusable; caller-substituted vertex/texture buffers and original supplied pixels retain their separate ownership.",
    "Four new actual-object controls cover normal retirement, all destructor faults/public collection mutation, partial attribute-construction failure and source3 wrapper failure. Sixteen focused tests and owning live PBR GPU/composition/export groups verify closure and rendering."
  ],
  "qualification": "Current fast16 passes 4,208 units/411 files on held inputs16; focused unit7 passes 16 real-object controls across two files. All six current PBR browser groups pass: components/mips, shared world, standalone observation, composition/journal/artwork, normal export and actual mixed authenticated HTTP/replay. Source3 normal MP4s and six mixed raw HTTP bodies preserve preceding slice33 bytes. Initial fast8 failed prefer-const on a private identity that also needed retirement; clear that lookup slot on disposal, then rerun. Original browser suffix behind failure was unrun. Existing quotas/source schemas/render math unchanged. No new native2/depth/Node broad/installed/full gate claim; prior native2/depth source33 and installed b4fc65ed remain separately pinned. Application-visible owned backings retire; driver internals/process RSS and aggregate source/world/body/replay admission remain separate.",
